# Environment files
#
# `.env` is committed on purpose: Cloudflare Pages loads it while building, so
# the public origin reaches CI without dashboard configuration. `.env.development`
# and `.env.production` are committed too, since Vite reads them. All three are
# therefore public, and `npm run validate:env` fails the release gate if a
# secret ever lands in `.env`.
#
# Real credentials belong in a `*.local` file (never committed) or in the
# Cloudflare dashboard.
.env.local
.env.*.local

